", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bbea775e884bd8829609bdb5070953d3f32e922a2ba29246e5cf42a671882429","event_uuid":"d73a5b53-bdc1-4997-b19a-d293746ea19f","position":{"commit_sha":"48f63da5fa6d5c5b5e07d208c66a1dbcead616a4","position":"1785533446319981001-d73a5b53-bdc1-4997-b19a-d293746ea19f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"12f371d4f086e21d56f77ae27eb8c606d66379268b3bffdf76e4f877b4180787","event_uuid":"ee5e80df-d523-4258-b3ca-0c078a460946","position":{"commit_sha":"a02239e07a84b38a87eaa3d4545ae4a7217f5d78","position":"1785533707846930492-ee5e80df-d523-4258-b3ca-0c078a460946"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"2e857a0a-03b6-414c-b41a-2fd1809c94b8","comments":[],"created_at":1785510695401554001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b560f9cf-f1ed-48bc-af76-7722902670ae","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8ce0-881f-761f-4f0d"}],"description":"# Guard the provider session: wrap run() in `with ProviderSession(...)`\n\nADR 0056 decision 2. A CORRECTNESS fix, not a refactor — independently valuable, and it should land\neven if the rest of the decomposition is descoped.\n\n## The defect (RE-MEASURED at c1fc3cee4, after e6bd and 8229 landed)\n\n    runner.py:294   provider_session = ProviderSession(cfg)   # its builders open httpx clients\n    runner.py:445   try:                                       # <-- guard starts 151 lines later\n    runner.py:495   finally:\n    runner.py:501       provider_session.close()\n\nLines 294–444 sit OUTSIDE the guard, and code in that window raises BY DESIGN:\n`_check_tool_capability(...)` is called at runner.py:337 and raises `LLMConfigError`. Anything\nraising there leaks an opened `httpx.AsyncClient` — one per affected call.\n\n`ProviderSession.__enter__` / `__exit__` ALREADY EXIST at **providers.py:323 and :326** and are\nnever used: `grep -c 'with ProviderSession' src/rebar/llm/runner.py` returns 0. Meanwhile\nproviders.py:18–24 documents \"`runner.run()` wraps its body in `with ProviderSession(cfg) as\nsession:`\" — a caller that does not exist. This ticket makes that docstring true.\n\nNOTE ON COORDINATES: an earlier version of this plan cited 301/474/582 for the three sites and\nproviders.py:295–299 for the dunders. Those were correct when written and are now ALL STALE — e6bd\nremoved the except spine and 8229 removed the settings block, shifting everything. The numbers above\nare re-measured at c1fc3cee4. **Re-locate by CONTENT, not by these offsets** if the base moves again.\n\n## Approach\n\nMove construction into a `with` covering provider resolution through the call and teardown, and drop\nthe now-redundant `finally: provider_session.close()` — `__exit__` owns it. Preserve the existing\nbest-effort semantics (close logs, never raises).\n\nCONSTRAINT: `assert_gated(\"agentic filesystem tools\")` at **runner.py:261** is a FAIL-CLOSED security\ncheck and MUST stay AHEAD of provider construction. Do not reorder it into the guarded region in a\nway that opens a client before the refusal path runs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — the `with`, and removal of the redundant `finally`.\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py` — **REQUIRED, and this ticket owns it.**\n  See below; omitting it breaks that test at runtime.\n- `tests/unit/` — the leak test.\n\n### THIS TICKET OWNS ONE STUB REPAIR — it is not optional and not a \"later child\" problem\n\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py:111` defines `_NoBuildProviderSession` and\ninstalls it at :124 via `monkeypatch.setattr(runner_mod, \"ProviderSession\", _NoBuildProviderSession)`.\nMEASURED: that stub implements `__init__`, `supports`, `is_resolvable` and `close` — and **NOT**\n`__enter__` / `__exit__`. The moment `run()` says `with ProviderSession(cfg) as ...`, the stub stops\nsatisfying the context-manager protocol and that test fails at runtime.\n\n**Add `__enter__` (returning `self`) and `__exit__` (calling `self.close()`) to that stub IN THE SAME\nCOMMIT as the `with`.** This is a stub gaining the protocol the real object already has\n(providers.py:323/326) — NOT a weakened assertion, so it is compatible with the \"no test ASSERTION\nchanged\" criterion.\n\nThis is a DIFFERENT failure mode from the six `monkeypatch.setattr` rebind hazards the parent story\ndocuments: nothing moved modules here, so re-importing a name fixes nothing. The stub's INTERFACE\nfell behind the call site. Do not go looking for a module-globals explanation.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tier with a stubbed builder recording opens/closes; no network.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a test asserts that when the pre-call window raises (e.g. `_check_tool_capability`), the\n      session's client is STILL closed — this test FAILS against today's code, so it cannot pass\n      vacuously\n- [ ] a test asserts the happy path closes EXACTLY once (a `with` plus a leftover `finally` would\n      double-close, which the stub must be able to detect)\n- [ ] `grep -c 'with ProviderSession' src/rebar/llm/runner.py` is 1, so providers.py:18–24 no longer\n      documents an absent caller\n- [ ] a close that raises is still logged and never propagated (best-effort semantics unchanged)\n- [ ] `_NoBuildProviderSession` in `tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py` gains\n      `__enter__`/`__exit__` in THIS commit, and that test file passes\n- [ ] `assert_gated(\"agentic filesystem tools\")` still executes BEFORE any provider client is\n      constructed — asserted by a test in which the gate refuses and NO client is opened, so the\n      fail-closed ordering is proven rather than assumed\n- [ ] the full suite passes with no test ASSERTION weakened, skipped or deleted","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"wrap the run body in with ProviderSession(cfg) as the guard, and drop the now-redundant finally: provider_session.close()"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_execution_mode_dispatch.py","reason":"the _NoBuildProviderSession stub at :111 has __init__/supports/is_resolvable/close but NO __enter__/__exit__; the with statement breaks it, so this child owns adding them in the SAME commit"},{"path":"tests/unit/","reason":"a test asserting a raise in the pre-call window still closes the client, which fails against todays code"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","7f86-d935-3742-476a"],["relates_to","8ce0-881f-761f-4f0d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"7f86-d935-3742-476a","parent_status_uuid":"a05e599b-7831-4628-9798-5883cd6863d1","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"a49e-3a93-9399-4756","ticket_type":"task","title":"Guard the provider session with a context manager in run()","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3aa360e2-a1ac-4064-8a67-7894e5568d8e","eb95ba13-be90-4c28-b575-c98aca693a6a","099cd738-5ec7-4582-9ccb-2d5869bae421","86856975-7cab-48c4-988c-e231a697450f","816bdbdd-43b5-484e-9d6c-b4f3dc694329","31606532-551a-450b-882e-afcce3a58759","70ca303d-5438-4d11-bebd-48e982582472","a05e599b-7831-4628-9798-5883cd6863d1","d73a5b53-bdc1-4997-b19a-d293746ea19f","ee5e80df-d523-4258-b3ca-0c078a460946","b560f9cf-f1ed-48bc-af76-7722902670ae"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785535824105979764,"uuid":"d6d592f3-5c4d-4160-871e-0cb585167179"}